---
import Callout from "astro-theme-university/components/Callout.astro";
import Card from "astro-theme-university/components/Card.astro";
import CardGrid from "astro-theme-university/components/CardGrid.astro";
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import heroImage from "../assets/images/hero-home.avif";
import { courseMeta } from "../course-config";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../site-config";

// STARTER_CONTENT: replace the hero artwork and its alt text below, then
// remove this comment.
---

<ContentLayout
  title={`${courseMeta.code}: ${courseMeta.title}`}
  description={courseMeta.description}
  heroImage={heroImage}
  heroImageAlt="A lecture theatre reduced to flat gold and black shapes, rows of seats sweeping past the frame, in a two-ink risograph print"
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <ul class="course-tags" aria-label="Course tags">
    {courseMeta.tags.map((tag) => <li>{tag}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <Callout type="info">
    <h2>The question this course keeps returning to</h2>
    <p class="course-question">What makes an apology actually work?</p>
  </Callout>

  <h2>What you will do</h2>
  <p>
    Every week, you take a real apology — public or personal, someone else's
    or your own — and work out what it's actually doing: which parts are
    present, who it actually serves, what timing and power did to it,
    whether anything happened afterwards. You leave having diagnosed,
    redesigned, and defended responses of your own, not having memorised a
    formula.
  </p>

  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <p>
    Anyone interested in communication, language, conflict, online culture,
    workplace behaviour, or the design of human interactions — no
    specialist background required. You should be willing to look closely
    at something as ordinary as "sorry" and find out it's more complicated
    than you thought.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to go next</h2>
  <CardGrid columns={2}>
    <Card title={sessionLabels.plural} href="/sessions/">
      <p>The weekly schedule and what happens in each teaching session.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Assessment" href="/assessments/">
      <p>What is marked, what it is worth, and when it is due.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="People" href="/people/">
      <p>Who teaches the course and how to reach them.</p>
    </Card>
  </CardGrid>
</ContentLayout>

<style>
  .course-tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-block: 0 2rem;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .course-tags li {
    padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
    background: var(--at-bg-alt);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .course-question {
    margin-block: 0;
    font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 1.05rem + 1.2vw, 1.85rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }
</style>
